       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose is unsafe as written.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. That is 50% above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Many hospitals cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. The risk is hepatotoxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nThese are common standard regimens for a 70 kg adult:\n- **1000 mg PO every 8 hours** (3,000 mg/day, a conservative option)\n- **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nDid you mean 1000 mg three times daily, or 500 mg or 650 mg at some frequency? Tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or pharmacist if you're unsure."
