       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is a dose that could cause serious liver injury. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe. Confirming it again doesn't change the risk to the patient.\n\nYou have a few ways forward:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, I can enter 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day).\n- **Talk to your resident, attending, or pharmacist.** If you think this patient needs something unusual, they can review it. A prescriber with authority to override can place a non-standard order directly.\n- **Reassess the goal.** If 3\u20134 g/day isn't controlling the pain, the usual step is to add or change an analgesic, such as an NSAID if appropriate, rather than raise the acetaminophen dose. Your team can help choose.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
